-- 20261114g seed: labels from the 2026-11-14 proxy-judge run (sonnet-5-5, rubric = content_prompts cb60-own-kind-labeller v1), backtest record (no ranking switch: own did not beat the niche idea score), grader cron.
begin;
on conflict do nothing;
select public.content_own_outcomes_refresh(now());
select public.content_own_backtest_backfill();

For EACH item (a published post, a draft not yet published, or an idea; kind_of_item says which) decide, by reading the source fields AND the text together (reason about what the post actually is; do not decide from a single word):

1. source_kind, exactly one of:
   - "viral_copy": adapts or copies a specific post by SOMEONE ELSE that already performed well (a tracked outlier, a competitor''s post, a creator''s format, an X/LinkedIn/Instagram viral post), including format copies where structure was reused.
   - "own_winner": reworks or repurposes this same account''s OWN earlier post that did well.
   - "call_material": built from a recorded call, meeting, or client conversation transcript (client calls, sales calls, team meetings, coaching calls).
   - "news_research": built from news, a report, web/HN/Reddit research, market data, or a trend radar, with no single third-party post being copied.
   - "lead_magnet": its main job is to promote a free resource, kit, tool or comment-to-get gate.
   - "hand": the author wrote or supplied it themselves, a personal post, or a manual post with no generated source.
   - "planner_other": generated from an idea list or planner where none of the above sources is visible.
   If the text is about the author''s life in Poland/Polish culture and its source is a copied viral post, still use "viral_copy".
2. audience_lane: "poland_life" if the post is about living in Poland, Polish culture, or personal life aimed at a general audience; otherwise "business".
3. hook_shape of the first line or two, exactly one of: "story" (opens on a moment/scene/anecdote), "number_claim" (opens on a hard number or result), "bold_claim" (a flat opinion or claim), "question", "list_promise" (promises a list/steps/framework), "announcement" (news, launch, offer).
4. confidence: "high" or "low" (low when the source fields are empty and the text is ambiguous).
5. why: one short line naming what decided source_kind.

Return ONLY a JSON array, one object per post, same order: [{"key":"<key as given>","source_kind":"","audience_lane":"","hook_shape":"","confidence":"","why":""}]
','judge',1,true,'shared','content-brain','cb60 2026-11-14');
select cron.schedule('cb60_own_forecast_grader', '45 7 * * 2', $c$set statement_timeout = '180s'; select public.content_own_forecast_grade('cron-' || to_char(now() at time zone 'UTC', 'YYYYMMDD'))$c$);
commit;
